From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: make existing audio sync calculations testable off-device

Move the existing error accumulator into a header with its timer supplied as a
type. Production still uses XbmcThreads::EndTime; native tests can advance time
without sleeping or linking the player, renderer, ALSA or an Amlogic driver.

Extract the residual-acquisition settling and magnitude tests unchanged. Keep
clock access, short-circuit guards, correction ownership and application in
the player. In particular preserve the existing value-based freshness rule
and strict thresholds so its later fix is a separate, testable behavior change.

These shared-code moves are necessary because the actual synchronization
calculations live in AudioEngine and VideoPlayer, not the AML consumers. The
native harness compiles these production headers, not a separate sync model.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

